toMilesPerHour method:

Check if the kilometersPerHour parameter is less than 0. If it is, return -1 as an indication of an invalid value.

Otherwise, calculate the conversion from kilometers per hour to miles per hour using the formula kilometersPerHour / 1.609. You can use the Math.round method to round the result to the nearest whole number and return it.

printConversion method:

First, check if the kilometersPerHour parameter is less than 0. If it is, print "Invalid Value" to the console, and then use the return statement to exit the method.

If the value is valid, call the toMilesPerHour method to convert kilometersPerHour to miles per hour and store the result in a variable, say milesPerHour.

Finally, use System.out.println to print the conversion result to the console in the format: kilometersPerHour + " km/h = " + milesPerHour + " mi/h".